n and stale coverage snapshots addresses this dependent failure without weakening the required check.","decision":"fix","evidence":["##[group]Run exit 1","##[error]Process completed with exit code 1."],"key":"check:114962676539"},{"analysis":"All three MongoDB standalone-library packages use the no-argument createCommandListener(), which cannot derive the configured server target under stable database conventions. Every operation and endSessions therefore lacks server.address and server.port. The pinned 2.32.0-alpha library exposes createCommandListener(List<ServerAddress>); the fix supplies the complete seed list from each driver's configured MongoClientSettings, preserving the existing exact server assertions. Three seed-propagation regressions pass, and real library OTLP probes reproduce the missing attributes without seeds and verify corrected span and duration attributes with seeds for all three driver versions. Frozen CI also records missing service.instance coverage in the three library snapshots and network.peer attributes in the synchronous agent duration snapshot; those observations are incorporated. Docker scenarios could not be rerun here, and four Weaver-dependent Python tests were skipped, as detailed in diagnostics.","decision":"fix","evidence":["find: db.system.name='mongodb', db.operation.name='find': server.address expected '127.0.0.1' on every span, saw [None]","aggregate: db.system.name='mongodb', db.operation.name='endSessions': server.port expected on every span, set on 0/1","the committed data.json files are out of date","diff --git a/scenarios/database/java/mongodb/sync/opentelemetry-javaagent/data.json b/scenarios/database/java/mongodb/sync/opentelemetry-javaagent/data.json","\"service.instance.id\""],"key":"check:114955855007"}],"input_identity":{"pr_diff_sha256":"5596a4aaa7764a7a4daa641093c7fcf11209b1d7ec2704d1667eaa7526740bf5"},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"2c99115562b0a4769efe85000e50ef48cc56934e33032ba47dd7181dfb6c23c3","rerun_run